{"rules":[{"jurisdiction":"CA","level":"state","category":"screening_restrictions","status":"in_force","title":"California Civil Rights Council regulations on criminal history in housing decisions","requirement":"Regulations limit what type of criminal history may be sought, how an applicant's criminal history can be considered, and what actions a landlord may take based on it. Blanket bans on applicants with a criminal record are prohibited, as are policies that consider arrests without convictions. Landlords are not entirely barred from checking criminal history.","key_value":"Blanket bans on applicants with a criminal record prohibited; arrests without convictions may not be considered","coverage_conditions":"Housing decisions generally; no building-level coverage limits stated","exemptions":null,"coverage_logic":{"covers":null,"exempt":null},"subject":"landlord","interaction":null,"yields_to_local":false,"preempts_local":false,"effective_date":"2020-01-01","effective_rule":null,"enacted_date":"2019","end_date":null,"penalty":null,"citation":"California Civil Rights Council (formerly Fair Employment and Housing Council) regulations on use of criminal history in housing, effective Jan. 1, 2020","quoted_span":"Blanket bans on applicants with a criminal record are prohibited, as are policies that consider arrests without convictions.","supporting_spans":["The California regulations include limits on what type of criminal history may be sought, how an applicant’s criminal history can be considered, and what actions a landlord may take based on an applicant’s criminal history."],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_note":null},{"jurisdiction":"CA","level":"state","category":"screening_restrictions","status":"in_force","title":"SB 329: source of income includes government housing subsidies (\"No Section 8\" policies prohibited)","requirement":"SB 329 updated the FEHA definition of \"source of income\" to include government housing subsidy programs such as Section 8. State law prohibits landlords from refusing to participate in such programs, so \"No Section 8\" policies are unlawful.","key_value":"Refusing Section 8 / government housing subsidy participation is prohibited","coverage_conditions":"All landlords subject to FEHA; no building-level coverage limits stated","exemptions":null,"coverage_logic":{"covers":null,"exempt":null},"subject":"landlord","interaction":null,"yields_to_local":false,"preempts_local":false,"effective_date":"2020-01-01","effective_rule":null,"enacted_date":"2019","end_date":null,"penalty":"The California Civil Rights Department is enforcing, including by filing lawsuits against offending landlords","citation":"SB 329 (2019) (Fair Employment and Housing Act)","quoted_span":"This change meant that, as of Jan. 1, 2020, state law prohibits landlords from refusing to participate in such programs.","supporting_spans":["Despite being the law since January 2020, some landlords continue to have “No Section 8” policies in place, and the California Civil Rights Department (CRD) is cracking down on violators."],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_note":null},{"jurisdiction":"CA","level":"state","category":"screening_restrictions","status":"in_force","title":"SB 267: limits on credit history use for applicants with government rental subsidies","requirement":"Rental property owners may not use a person's credit history as part of the application process if the applicant has a government rental subsidy such as Section 8, without offering the applicant the option to provide alternative evidence of a verifiable legal means to pay their portion of the rent.","key_value":"Must offer alternative evidence of ability to pay the tenant's portion of rent when using credit history for subsidized applicants","coverage_conditions":"Applicants with a government rental subsidy such as Section 8","exemptions":null,"coverage_logic":{"covers":null,"exempt":null},"subject":"landlord","interaction":null,"yields_to_local":false,"preempts_local":false,"effective_date":null,"effective_rule":null,"enacted_date":null,"end_date":null,"penalty":null,"citation":"SB 267 (amending FEHA)","quoted_span":"to prohibit rental property owners from using a person’s credit history as part of the application process – if they have a government rental subsidy, such as Section 8 — without offering the applicant the option to provide alternative evidence of a verifiable legal means to pay their portion of the rent.","supporting_spans":[],"confidence":0.6,"conflict_note":null}],"notes":"Only screening_restrictions rules are described; the document has no rent increase, just cause, deposit, fee or algorithmic pricing content. No statutory or regulatory section numbers are given, so citations use bill or regulation names. SB 267's enactment and effective dates are not stated (\"last year's\"), so they are null. Status is in_force on the assumption it was enacted before the query date. Federal HUD guidance is ignored as out of scope."}
